  "captured_regression_assertions": [
    "A known permutation and positive scale gauge is recovered with a finite assignment gap exceeding the frozen literal threshold by more than the numerical guard. The legacy matcher returns that known gauge and its two existing diagnostic keys in this case.",
    "Transport of one literal mixed-layer edit reaches the expected target parent hash. Exact rational scores of the edited source and transported edit equal separately specified expectations at four handcrafted inputs.",
    "Renumbering the separated source and target produces the expected transformed gauge and preserves the assignment gap within the asserted numerical-guard tolerance.",
    "The regression exhaustively enumerates an independently specified three-by-three integer cost matrix. Checked best and alternative objectives match its first two assignments, including a cheapest alternative that retains one selected edge. Literal thresholds accept clear separation and abstain both inside the guard and at equality.",
    "Two duplicated-feature parents have equal exact scores at one literal input, while the legacy matching choice gives a different edited score; transport by the known gauge reproduces the specified edited score. This illustrates ambiguity in edit correspondence.",
    "Duplicate rows have zero assignment gap; a near-tie construction has positive gap below threshold despite large local row preferences. Both cases abstain, including after independent hidden renumbering, with gap agreement within the asserted guard tolerance.",
    "Zero incoming affine rows in the source, target or both produce abstention with unavailable gap and the expected zero-row diagnostics.",
    "One nonzero hidden unit returns its known scale with no_alternative gap status. Extreme large and small nonzero magnitudes abstain at incoming_norms with numerical_failure, unavailable gap and empty exact-zero row lists.",
    "The threshold argument is mandatory. Booleans, negative values, NaN, infinity, a string and a non-exactly-representable integer are rejected. All collected diagnostic mappings serialize with allow_nan=False, and each reported gap is finite or absent."
  ],
